ls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Laurel Lee (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Florida's 15th District, in the Tampa Bay area, leans Republican by about nine points. Laurel Lee, first elected in 2022, is seeking a third term and turned back a primary challenge from Hernando County commissioner Steve Champion. Democrat Robert People won his party's nomination in August but enters the general election with minimal resources.\n\nLee has raised $2.3 million and holds $1.9 million on hand, compared with roughly $40,000 raised and $3,500 on hand for People. Every major race rater places the district on the Republican-safe side of the board, and House Democrats dropped it from their targeted seats list in July. Betting markets give People about an eight percent chance of an upset. No public general-election polls are available, so the forecast rests on district fundamentals, the money gap, and expert consensus, all of which point to a comfortable Republican hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0439, "margin": -10.97}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0254, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0439, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0149, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0408, "margin": -12.0}]}